.TH KROUTON 1 "November 2026" "Krouton 1.0.0" "macOS Optical Mastering Manual"
.SH NAME
krouton \- macOS optical media mastering studio and headless CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B krouton
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B krouton
is a native macOS optical disc authoring, archival rescue, multi-disc spanning, and inspection suite supporting Red Book CD-DA, Hybrid UDF/ISO-9660/Joliet Data, DVD-Video, AVCHD-on-DVD, Blu-ray, and BDXL (up to 128 GB).
When invoked without arguments,
.B krouton
launches the interactive SwiftUI workspace. When invoked with a subcommand, it executes headlessly on the terminal.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B drives [--json]
List connected USB, SATA, FireWire, and Thunderbolt optical drives, firmware revisions, ATIP/MID manufacturer codes, and free LBA sectors.
.TP
.B formats [--json]
List all supported optical mastering workflows and compatible target disc sizes.
.TP
.B inspect IfileR [--sha256] [--json]
Inspect an .iso, .dmg, .bin, or .cue disc image for El Torito / Apple Partition Map bootability, filesystems, 2048-byte LBA sectors, and SHA-256 digest.
.TP
.B span [--medium IsizeR] Ifiles...R [--json]
Calculate a multi-disc spanning plan across target media capacities (cd650, cd700, cd800, minidvd, dvd5, dvd9, bd25, bd50, bdxl100, bdxl128).
.TP
.B iso -V ItitleR -o Ioutput.isoR Isource-dirR
Master a hybrid UDF + ISO-9660 + Joliet optical disc image from a source folder.
.TP
.B completions Izsh|bash|fishR
Output shell tab-completion script for the specified shell.
